title: Rosa Luxemburg
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: luxemburg_advisor = 1 and luxemburg_alive = 1
new-page: true

= Rosa Luxemburg

The party's leading theorist. She believes the revolution must be the work of the majority of the working class, not of a putsch, and she distrusts the Bolsheviks' methods.

- @persuade
- @against_putsch
- @root: Return to main

@persuade
title: Win the Argument
subtitle: Raises every district's loyalty to the Zentrale.
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next advisor action.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 8;
}
!}

Luxemburg speaks and writes tirelessly. Even her opponents in the districts read her.

@against_putsch
title: Against Putschism
subtitle: Lowers militancy; the ultra-left is offended.
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next advisor action.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; last_advisor_action = 1; militancy -= 10; repression -= 5; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 8; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5

A revolution cannot be ordered from above, Luxemburg argues. It must grow.
